! 43edo
!
43-tone equal tempered scale consisting of 43 sonically equal divisions per octave. Similar to 1/5-Syntonic Comma Meantone, the system was described by Joseph Sauveur in 1696. Step-size (named méride by Sauveur) is 27.9 cents.
